cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, or any number produced by it, please cite the SWITCH+
  workshop paper under `preferred-citation`.
title: >-
  Voxels or Millimetres? A Controlled Comparison of Lesion-Size Filtering for
  Native-Space Stroke Segmentation
abstract: >-
  Source code for a controlled comparison of voxel-count versus
  millimetre-cubed lesion-size filtering in native-space stroke lesion
  segmentation: the ISLES'26 submission container, the nnU-Net training and
  dataset-conversion code, and the measurement scripts. Pooled out-of-fold over
  1,453 subjects the shipped model reaches Dice 0.6552, Detection F1 0.6063 and
  PR-AUC 0.7617; filtering at all moves Detection F1 from 0.5333 to 0.5895, and
  at matched magnitude a mm^3 threshold beats a voxel-count threshold by 0.0036
  Detection F1 (95% CI [0.0016, 0.0058]).
